  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_020, acc=0.713) uses multimodal + multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion with scvi_n200/resnet50. The progression from single→multiprofile (+0.138) and avgpool→transformer (+0.035) shows strong gains from richer architecture. The fusion strategy (weighted vs. concat) is the one untested variable within this exact architecture. Question: Does concat fusion outperform weighted fusion when combining RNA and image features after transformer-based multiprofile aggregation? This is a single-variable change from the current best, so any accuracy difference is cleanly attributable to the fusion method. Why this experiment: It is the cheapest and most direct way to reduce uncertainty about an important design choice while preserving the proven multiprofile+transformer backbone. Expected cost is very similar to config_020 (~6.2 GPU hours, same encoders and aggregation), keeping total spend around ~19 GPU hours and leaving ample budget for 5 further experiments. If concat wins, it opens a new axis of improvement; if weighted holds, we confirm the current best and can pivot to testing a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) or alternative RNA encoder in subsequent runs."
}

